<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Chapter IV — The Archive</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500;600;700&family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --parchment: #ece1c4;
    --parchment-dark: #ddcda3;
    --page-edge: #c9b784;
    --ink: #3a2a1c;
    --ink-dim: #6b5738;
    --leather: #4a2f22;
    --leather-dark: #2e1c14;
    --gold: #9c7a2e;
    --flame: #b5502e;
    --font-display: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --font-body: "EB Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    --font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, monospace;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--leather-dark);
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(circle at 20% 10%, rgba(156,122,46,0.10), transparent 55%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 85% 90%, rgba(181,80,46,0.08), transparent 50%);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 44px 18px;
  }

  .book {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 620px;
    background: var(--parchment);
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at top left, rgba(255,255,255,0.15), transparent 40%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse at bottom right, rgba(0,0,0,0.06), transparent 45%);
    border: 1px solid var(--page-edge);
    border-radius: 3px;
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 0 var(--page-edge),
      0 4px 0 var(--parchment-dark),
      0 34px 60px -24px rgba(0,0,0,0.65);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .chapter-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 18px 30px;
    background: var(--leather);
    border-bottom: 3px double var(--gold);
  }

  .chapter-bar .roman {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    color: var(--parchment-dark);
  }

  .chapter-bar .flicker {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #c7a862;
  }

  .content {
    padding: 34px 34px 30px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 34px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: var(--leather);
  }

  p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  p.lede {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--flame);
    background: rgba(74,47,34,0.07);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .divider {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 28px 0 22px;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .divider::before, .divider::after {
    content: "";
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--page-edge);
  }
  .divider span {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .entry {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .entry:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 8px; }

  .entry h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 23px;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    color: var(--leather);
  }

  .entry .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }

  .entry p {
    font-size: 16.5px;
  }

  .spellbook {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    background: var(--leather-dark);
    color: #e9dcb8;
    border: 1px solid #1c110b;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 10px 0 4px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .spellbook .kw { color: #c7a862; }
  .spellbook .var { color: #7fb5a3; }
  .spellbook .str { color: #d99a6c; }
  .spellbook .cm { color: #7d7a6a; }
  .spellbook .out { color: #9aa88f; white-space: normal; }

  .nav-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 30px;
    padding-top: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--page-edge);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .nav-row a {
    color: var(--leather);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .nav-row a:hover { color: var(--flame); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="book">
    <div class="chapter-bar">
      <span class="roman">CHAPTER IV</span>
      <span class="flicker">by candlelight</span>
    </div>

    <div class="content">
      <h1>The Archive</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Past the fork, the path opens into a quiet room lined floor to
        ceiling with shelves. No doors to open here, no incantations
        to test — only scrolls, each holding one small rule of the
        old language, left behind for anyone who wants to read before
        they continue.
      </p>

      <p>
        Take your time. Nothing in this room asks anything of you.
      </p>

      <div class="divider"><span>the scrolls</span></div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h2>print()</h2>
        <p class="kicker">speaks something aloud</p>
        <p>
          Whatever sits inside the parentheses is revealed exactly as
          written — this is how the language shows you anything at
          all. Without it, a spell may do something, but no one would
          ever see the result.
        </p>
        <div class="spellbook"><span class="kw">print</span>(<span class="str">"The lantern flickers."</span>)
<span class="out">The lantern flickers.</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h2>name = value</h2>
        <p class="kicker">gives something a name to remember it by</p>
        <p>
          This is a <code>variable</code>. Once a name holds a value,
          you can use that name anywhere you'd otherwise have to
          repeat the value itself — and if the value changes later,
          everything using that name changes with it.
        </p>
        <div class="spellbook"><span class="var">torches_lit</span> = <span class="str">3</span>
<span class="kw">print</span>(<span class="var">torches_lit</span>)
<span class="out">3</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h2>"quotation marks"</h2>
        <p class="kicker">seals plain text so it isn't mistaken for a name</p>
        <p>
          Anything wrapped in quotes — single or double, the house
          doesn't mind which — is treated as exact text, called a
          <code>string</code>. Without the quotes, the language
          assumes you're speaking the name of something, not the
          words themselves.
        </p>
        <div class="spellbook"><span class="str">"door"</span>    <span class="cm"># the word "door" itself</span>
door       <span class="cm"># the thing named door, wherever that is</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h2># comments</h2>
        <p class="kicker">notes left for a reader, not the house</p>
        <p>
          Anything after a <code>#</code> on a line is ignored — the
          house never hears it. It exists only for whoever reads the
          scroll later, to explain what a spell is doing and why.
        </p>
        <div class="spellbook"><span class="cm"># checks whether the door should open</span>
<span class="kw">if</span> <span class="var">age</span> &gt;= <span class="var">18</span>:</div>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h2>indentation</h2>
        <p class="kicker">shows what belongs to what</p>
        <p>
          A line indented beneath another belongs to it — it only
          happens as part of that line above. You saw this at the
          fork: the message beneath <code>if</code> only spoke when
          the condition above it was true. The house is strict about
          this; an unindented line stands on its own.
        </p>
        <div class="spellbook"><span class="kw">if</span> <span class="var">age</span> &gt;= <span class="var">18</span>:
    <span class="kw">print</span>(<span class="str">"You may pass"</span>)  <span class="cm"># belongs to the if</span>
<span class="kw">print</span>(<span class="str">"The torch still burns"</span>)  <span class="cm"># always runs</span></div>
      </div>

      <p>
        That's all the room has to offer for now. When you're ready,
        the path continues.
      </p>

      <div class="nav-row">
        <a href="lesson3.html">&larr; Chapter III</a>
        <span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>